      "text": [
        " «عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يُضَحِّيَ عَنْهُمْ» قُلْتُ فَإِنَّهُ أَعْطَاهُمْ دَرَاهِمَ فَبَعْضُهُمْ ضَحَّى وَ بَعْضُهُمْ أَمْسَكَ اَلدَّرَاهِمَ وَ صَامَ قَالَ «قَدْ أَجْزَأَ عَنْهُمْ وَ هُوَ بِالْخِيَارِ إِنْ شَاءَ تَرَكَهَا » قَالَ قَالَ «وَ لَوْ أَنَّهُ أَمَرَهُمْ فَصَامُوا كَانَ قَدْ أَجْزَأَ عَنْهُمْ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2897 - It was narrated that Sama'ah asked Imam (as) about a man who instructed his servants to perform Tamattu‘ (Umrah and Hajj combined).\nImam (as) said: \"It is incumbent upon him to offer the sacrifice on their behalf.\"\nI said: \"What if he gave them dirhams, and some of them offered the sacrifice while others kept the dirhams and chose to fast?\"\nImam (as) said: \"It is sufficient for them, and he has the choice to leave it as is if he wishes.\"\nImam (as) further said: \"If he had commanded them to fast instead, it would have sufficed for them.\""
        ]
      }
    },
